# spark in newsboat -- your own AI, on your own machine
# (spark.forgewright.ai). Append this to your own ~/.newsboat/config:
#
#     cat ~/.newsboat/spark/config.spark >> ~/.newsboat/config
#
# The key is newsboat's macro prefix: , then s. The article you are on
# (open, or selected in the list) is piped to spark, the screen is
# spark's for the exchange, and Enter brings newsboat back exactly as
# it was:
#
#   Enter or ?         the overview: every line quotes the article,
#                      or an honest refusal -- the verdict
#   your words         a conversation: follow-ups ride the thread
#                      ("can you translate that?" has a that); an
#                      unheld quote is marked [not in the text]
#   after an answer    spark> again: follow up; Enter alone returns
#   Ctrl-C             never mind -- newsboat comes straight back
#
# A link feed's stub (a headline and pointers, no story) is named
# instead of asked: "this feed carried only a stub -- o opens the
# story in w3m; M-s asks there".
#
# Every line of the answer quotes the article; when the article does
# not answer, the reply is one line showing its own opening words --
# never a guess. spark-newsboat is this repository's wrapper around
# `spark read`: it draws the prompt on the terminal newsboat hands
# over, folds spark's stderr into the answer (a refusal shows instead
# of vanishing) and wraps long lines at spaces (SPARK_NEWSBOAT_WIDTH,
# default 78). Nothing leaves this machine but the rendered article
# and your words, to the brain spark is configured for. Needs newsboat
# 2.10 or newer and spark 1.20 or newer.
macro s pipe-to "spark-newsboat --ask"
# newsboat 2.38 or newer can put it on spark's key in every app,
# Alt-s, beside the macro -- uncomment:
# bind <ESC>s article,articlelist pipe-to "spark-newsboat --ask" -- "spark"
